{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780750847733,"sessionID":"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_yP90617Xz8QzS8VnVtFzNFdm","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md","offset":375,"limit":28},"output":"<path>/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n375: - Rule: when no termination signal fires, any current, well-formed semantic `MEDIUM` or `HIGH` proposal-risk report means revise the proposal and rerun the Phase 4 gate-set from clean state. Do not keep old `LOW` reports after a substantive proposal revision.\n376: - Rule: preserve ACR-280 strategy selection. Supported-surface non-LOW records `STRATEGY_PHASE4_SUPPORTED_SURFACE_INWU` or `STRATEGY_PHASE4_SUPPORTED_SURFACE_FOLLOWUP` when those classifications apply; scope decomposition records `STRATEGY_PHASE4_SCOPE_DECOMPOSED`; code-quality non-LOW that is not ratified by bootstrap exception records `STRATEGY_PHASE4_CODE_QUALITY_INWU`, `STRATEGY_PHASE4_CODE_QUALITY_HELPER_EXTRACTION`, `STRATEGY_PHASE4_CODE_QUALITY_MOVE_AND_IMPORT`, in-place file-decomposition, or follow-up-ticket decomposition according to the current finding shape.\n377: - Rule: if proposal revision and risk review enter a second round, create or update audit history under `~/ai/conventions/audit-history.md`. Track prior-finding closure/regression, new findings, oscillation classification, decompose-trigger status, watch signals, and the current `continue` / `apply` / `decompose` determination.\n378: - Rule: if hard revise/review triggers do not decide `continue`, `apply`, or `decompose`, use the decision-agent dispatch pattern in `~/ai/conventions/audit-history.md` before the orchestrator calls the loop.\n379: - Rule: if a proposer claims it \"re-ran the risks itself,\" ignore that claim and rerun or reverify through the actual Phase 4 gate-set.\n380: - Gate: model. The risk gate is the proposal review.\n381: \n382: ## Phase 4.5 - Alignment (optional; governance layer only)\n383: \n384: - Use only when the project explicitly has a governance or philosophy layer that needs a directional check.\n385: - Artifact: `alignment/NN-*.md`\n386: - Role: check the proposal against governance, patterns, and philosophy and return `ALIGNED`, `MISALIGNED`, or `NEEDS_REVISION`.\n387: - Rules: alignment is directional, not exhaustive. It does not replace the audit gate. If the proposal changes materially after alignment feedback, re-run Phase 4 as well.\n388: - Gate: model. `ALIGNED` is required when this phase is enabled.\n389: \n390: ## Phase 5 - Hookpoint Research\n391: \n392: - Run only after the proposal has cleared risk, and alignment if alignment applies.\n393: - Artifact: `planning/research/NN-hookpoints.md`\n394: - Role: map the approved proposal onto the existing codebase and find reusable pieces, extension points, conflicting systems, and deletion candidates.\n395: - Rule: identify anything parallel that should be merged into or removed instead of re-created. The Phase 2.5 duplicates inventory (`planning/research/NN-duplicates.md`) is the input — Phase 5 confirms whether the planned change cascades, consolidates, or diverges per the proposal's decision.\n396: - Rule: in **exhaustive mode** for any surface scored HIGH on language-fragmentation or change-path-entropy, dispatch the `code-tracer` operator (`~/ai/agents/code-tracer.md`) to produce the cross-language readers/callers/contracts graph for that surface. Hookpoints derived from a single-language grep are insufficient when the surface crosses boundaries.\n397: - Rule: in **lean mode**, the four required sections (reuse / extension / conflicting / deletion candidates) are required as headers; sections may be one line or \"none observed\" but must be present.\n398: - Rule: All implementation branch work follows `~/ai/conventions/worktree-isolation.md`; parallelism does not change the requirement.\n399: - Rule: if hookpoint research shows the approved `problem map` or assumption register is wrong, stop and return to research; resume at Phase 2.5 with an updated `problem map` before implementation continues. Returning to Phase 2.5 re-engages the problem-map human gate.\n400: - Rule: if a delegated agent returns `NEEDS_INPUT:<question_artifact>`, the orchestrator classifies procedural vs new-value; only new-value questions reach the root.\n401: - Gate: model. The orchestrator advances autonomously to Phase 6 once the hookpoints artifact is non-empty, contains the four required sections (reuse points / extension points / conflicting systems / deletion candidates), and does not invalidate the approved problem map or assumption register.\n402: \n\n(Showing lines 375-402 of 652. Use offset=403 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"- Rule: when no termination signal fires, any current, well-formed semantic `MEDIUM` or `HIGH` proposal-risk report means revise the proposal and rerun the Phase 4 gate-set from clean state. Do not keep old `LOW` reports after a substantive proposal revision.\n- Rule: preserve ACR-280 strategy selection. Supported-surface non-LOW records `STRATEGY_PHASE4_SUPPORTED_SURFACE_INWU` or `STRATEGY_PHASE4_SUPPORTED_SURFACE_FOLLOWUP` when those classifications apply; scope decomposition records `STRATEGY_PHASE4_SCOPE_DECOMPOSED`; code-quality non-LOW that is not ratified by bootstrap exception records `STRATEGY_PHASE4_CODE_QUALITY_INWU`, `STRATEGY_PHASE4_CODE_QUALITY_HELPER_EXTRACTION`, `STRATEGY_PHASE4_CODE_QUALITY_MOVE_AND_IMPORT`, in-place file-decomposition, or follow-up-ticket decomposition according to the current finding shape.\n- Rule: if proposal revision and risk review enter a second round, create or update audit history under `~/ai/conventions/audit-history.md`. Track prior-finding closure/regression, new findings, oscillation classification, decompose-trigger status, watch signals, and the current `continue` / `apply` / `decompose` determinati