its the close-keyword footer itself.\n577: - Rule: RCA-track. The draft PR description includes before/after evidence for every Phase 0 red signal, whether a newly authored reproduction test or an existing failing test accepted as the reproduction signal: the red-run command and output or accepted failure evidence, paired with the matching post-fix green-run command and output recorded in Step 6c. Pass the evidence path(s) to `pr-writer` via `context_files` so they're folded into the body in audience-safe form.\n578: \n579: ## Phase 10 - Promote To Ready-For-Review\n580: \n581: - Automated by the orchestrator once Phase 9 succeeds and the Phase 8 process-tree audit has cleared.\n582: - Rule: the orchestrator runs `gh pr ready <pr_number>` and records the promotion in `${scratch_dir}/pr-promoted.txt`. No human gate.\n583: \n584: ## Gate Ownership\n585: \n586: See `~/ai/conventions/gate-ownership.md` for the phase-by-phase table.\n587: \n588: Rule of thumb:\n589: - the implementation-pipeline human gates are (1) the Phase 2.5 problem-map review and (2) legitimate NEEDS_INPUT new-value-question surfacing per `~/ai/agents/implementation-pipeline-orchestrator.md`\n590: - every other phase belongs to a model gate or to automation\n591: - the proposal is reviewed by the risk gate, not by an extra human approval pass\n592: - Phase 9 (draft PR) and Phase 10 (promotion) are both automated by the orchestrator\n593: \n594: ## Tiered Approval\n595: \n596: Anything with user-visible side effects follows `~/ai/workflows/tiered-approval.md`.\n597: \n598: Practical default:\n599: - drafting code is not Tier-3\n\n(Showing lines 523-599 of 652. Use offset=600 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"- `terminal_reason=no_value_provided` is accepted convergence when every actionable in-diff comment in the latest iteration was assessed `review_provided_value: false`.\n- `needs_caller_decision=true` surfaces valuable `rejected` or `deferred` per-comment outcomes to the root call